# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Refute configuration
#  Copy this file to .env and fill it in, then run:  npm run config
#  On Vercel, Netlify, GitHub Pages or Docker, set the same names as
#  environment variables instead (they override this file).
#
#  Everything here ends up in the public website, so NEVER put secret
#  keys in this file. The build refuses Supabase secret keys.
#
#  Your name, institution, AI key and model are set inside the app
#  (Settings), not here. The AI key is stored on the server only.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database (Supabase) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → Data API (URL) and → API Keys.
# Use the PUBLISHABLE key (sb_publishable_...). Older projects: the anon key.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=   (only if your project has no publishable key)

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rename the app if you like. Default: Refute
REFUTE_APP_NAME=Refute
# Link to the source code of the version you run (footer).
REFUTE_SOURCE_URL=

# ── Local server (npm run dev, npm start, Docker) ────────────────────
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=8000
